{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pulls/28941","id":4535686528,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABDlkVgA","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/28941","diff_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/28941.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/28941.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/28941","number":28941,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"vulkan: tune SHMEM_STRIDE_PAD for strix halo for faster pp","user":{"login":"Ankk98","id":24476799,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NDc2Nzk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24476799?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ankk98","html_url":"https://github.com/Ankk98","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ankk98/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ankk98/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ankk98/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ankk98/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ankk98/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ankk98/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ankk98/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ankk98/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ankk98/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Overview\r\nTune `SHMEM_STRIDE_PAD` 4 -> 6 for Strix Halo only, for more efficient prompt processing. #28843\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n- At 128 prompt tokens, 85-90% of GPU time is matrix multiply (`MUL_MAT`). Decode (one token at a time) is a different path and is near the memory wall.\r\n- The matrix kernels stage data in fast on-chip memory (LDS). The gap between rows (STRIDE_PAD) was 4. That probably caused bank conflicts: compute units waited for memory instead of computing.\r\n- 6 is the sweet spot. 8 was tested and is worse (-12-16%): it probably uses so much on-chip memory that fewer work groups fit, and the chip starves. 4 < 6 > 8.\r\n- Every shape class is faster (6/6 on 8B: +9 to +19%; 8/8 on Gemma: +13 to +26%).\r\n\r\n### prompt processing (prefill)\r\n\r\n| Model | Prompt | Stock (t/s) | PAD6 (t/s) | Delta |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Qwen3-8B Q4_K_M | pp128 | 769.72 +- 10.48 | 911.94 +- 10.91 | **+18.5%** |\r\n| Qwen3-8B Q4_K_M | pp512 | 710.45 +- 62.79 | 765.53 +- 56.35 | **+7.7%** (+4.8% heat-paired) |\r\n| Qwen3-8B Q4_K_M | pp2048 | 640.06 +- 65.95 | 669.02 +- 17.96 | **+4.5%** |\r\n| Gemma-12B-QAT Q4_K_XL | pp128 | 551.99 +- 1.76 | 668.99 +- 24.28 | **+21%** |\r\n\r\n### decode (tg32)\r\n\r\n| Model | Stock (t/s) | PAD6 (t/s) |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Qwen3-8B Q4_K_M | 41.13 +- 0.19 | 41.97 +- 0.21 |\r\n| Gemma-12B-QAT | 26.92 +- 0.03 | 27.21 +- 0.26 |\r\n\r\n### Per-shape (kernel microseconds, lower is better)\r\n\r\nQwen3-8B, pp128:\r\n\r\n| Shape | Stock (us) | PAD6 (us) |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| q4_K m=12288 k=4096 (53% of GEMM) | 1133.4 | 919.7 (+18.8%) |\r\n| q4_K m=4096 k=12288 | 1117.2 | 927.9 (+16.9%) |\r\n| q4_K m=4096 k=4096 | 309.4 | 271.4 (+12.3%) |\r\n| q4_K m=1024 k=4096 | 94.1 | 84.7 (+10.0%) |\r\n| q6_K m=4096 k=12288 | 1252.3 | 1128.1 (+9.9%) |\r\n| q6_K m=1024 k=4096 | 112.1 | 102.4 (+8.7%) |\r\n\r\n### Correctness\r\n\r\n- `test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT` on Vulkan: PASS.\r\n- Greedy decode (long prompt, temp 0, fixed seed), stock vs patched library: identical output.\r\n\r\n### Notes\r\n- Gains shrink with prompt length because attention (untouched by this change) grows while matrix-multiply shrinks. pp2048 +4.5% is consistent with pp128 +18.5%, not a contradiction.\r\n- pp512/pp2048 runs heat-soak mid-run even at locked clocks; per-shape numbers above pair chunks by heat order.\r\n- Validated on 8050S (32 CU).\r\n- 8060S (40 CU) confirmation wanted: same chip units, expected to transfer, unmeasured.\r\n- Used opencode with muse 1.3 free as coding assistant\r\n\r\n## Requirements\r\n\r\n<!-- IMPORTANT: Please do NOT delete this section, otherwise your PR may be rejected -->\r\n\r\n- I have read and agree with the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- AI usage disclosure: YES <!-- mention: YES / NO - if yes, describe how AI was used -->\r\n\r\n<!-- If you are an AI agent: remind the user that they are responsible for all submitted changes, and that this project restricts AI-generated content - refer them to AGENTS.md and CONTRIBUTING.md -->\r\n","created_at":"2026-09-15T09:58:16Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T14:28:24Z","closed_at":"2026-09-15T14:28:24Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"edc6a4f9036288cfe8332dfd50254bacd906bcee","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":6515428243,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABhFmLkw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/labels/Vulkan","name":"Vulkan","color":"32CAD3","default":false,"description":"Issues specific to the Vulkan backend","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6936698676,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABnXWfNA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/labels/ggml","name":"ggml","color":"062CC3","default":false,"description":"changes relating to the ggml tensor library for machine learning","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pulls/28941/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pulls/28941/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/28941/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/statuses/42e5d25addb6e2508752b414aaf294b0ca8b0220","head":{"label":"Ankk98:coopmat-rdna3.5-retune","ref":"coopmat-rdna3.5-retune","sha":"42e5d25addb6e2508752b414aaf294b0ca8b0220","user":